  "body": "The `currentTime` setter does change the official playback position: \"it must set the official playback position to the new value and then seek to the new value\"\n\nDoing nothing for `fastSeek()` seems like it would easily result in a UI that feels different compared to using `currentTime`.\n\n@jernoble, in the WebKit source it looks like this is actually handled similarly for `currentTime` and `fastSeek()`, with `m_lastSeekTime` being set for both. This isn't exactly the official playback position from the spec, but largely serves the same purpose.\n\nSo, should we change things so that [seek](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-media-seek) has a \"Set the _official_ playback position to the new playback position\" right before the async part?\n",
